    {
      "id": "q188-order",
      "source_numbers": ["188"],
      "view": {
        "mode": "single",
        "stem": "把表中按名次排列的五个队名看成一个有限数列。哪份说明正确描述了这个数列的首尾以及指定队名的相邻项？",
        "figure_ids": ["tbl-p0077-02"],
        "options": [
          {"id": "A", "text": "首项是 Westview，末项是 Harvest；Westview 的后一项是第 3 项 Zenith，Eastside 的前一项是第 2 项 Dawn。", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "B", "text": "首项是 Westview，末项是 Harvest；Westview 的后一项是第 2 项 Dawn，Eastside 的前一项是第 3 项 Zenith。", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "C", "text": "首项是 Harvest，末项是 Westview；Westview 的后一项是第 2 项 Dawn，Eastside 的前一项是第 3 项 Zenith。", "figure_ids": []}
        ]
      },
      "intent": {
        "task": "Read the finite sequence's boundary values and both immediate neighbor values with their positions.",
        "source_solution": "Positions 1..5 contain Westview,Dawn,Zenith,Eastside,Harvest. First Westview; last Harvest; the successor of Westview is position 2 Dawn; the predecessor of Eastside is position 3 Zenith.",
        "unit_reason": "One coherent order report checks boundaries and adjacency together; four separate value clicks would obscure the common positional relation.",
        "concept_blocks": [5,7,8,9],
        "limitations": ["Recognition does not demonstrate independently writing the four requested positional statements."],
        "figure_observations": [{"figure_id": "tbl-p0077-02", "observation": "Complete 640x320 preview shows a two-row table with header column and rank columns 1..5: Westview,Dawn,Zenith,Eastside,Harvest. Both far-right Harvest cell and bottom border are visible. Seeded SVG text and coordinates agree."}]
      },
      "key": {
        "correct": ["B"],
        "rationales": [
          {"option_id": "A", "truth": "incorrect", "derivation": "Taking any later team as a successor permits Zenith after Westview; taking any earlier team as a predecessor permits Dawn before Eastside, but neither is immediate.", "misconception": "Replace immediate adjacency by arbitrary later/earlier position, skipping Dawn after rank 1 and Zenith before rank 4."},
          {"option_id": "B", "truth": "correct", "derivation": "Read the first and fifth columns, then add 1 to Westview's index 1 and subtract 1 from Eastside's index 4.", "misconception": null},
          {"option_id": "C", "truth": "incorrect", "derivation": "The listed neighbors use increasing rank order, but the endpoints have been read in reverse; column 1 is not Harvest.", "misconception": "Interpret a larger numerical rank as earlier in the sequence only when choosing endpoints, reversing ranks 1 and 5."}
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "q189-length",
      "source_numbers": ["189"],
      "view": {
        "mode": "single",
        "stem": "把这一天按节次排列的课程看成有限数列。关于项数和相同项，哪项判断正确？",
        "figure_ids": ["tbl-p0078-01"],
        "options": [
          {"id": "A", "text": "有 5 项，第 3 项和第 4 项相同。", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "B", "text": "有 6 项，各项都不相同。", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "C", "text": "有 6 项，第 3 项和第 4 项相同。", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "D", "text": "有 7 项，第 3 项和第 4 项相同。", "figure_ids": []}
        ]
      },
      "intent": {
        "task": "Distinguish sequence length from the number of distinct values and locate repeated courses.",
        "source_solution": "Six positions contain Chemistry,Algebra,Literature,Literature,Drafting,PE. Positions 3 and 4 coincide in value; the range has five values, but the sequence has six terms.",
        "unit_reason": "Length and repetition are the same domain-versus-value distinction, so a complete judgment is the response unit.",
        "concept_blocks": [5,7,9],
        "limitations": ["Choosing a judgment does not demonstrate independently explaining why repeated values occupy distinct positions."],
        "figure_observations": [{"figure_id": "tbl-p0078-01", "observation": "Complete two-row table has header column Period/Subject and six numbered periods. Literature occurs in both columns 3 and 4. The rightmost period 6 PE cell and bottom edge are visible; the actual seeded SVG matches these labels."}]
      },
      "key": {
        "correct": ["C"],
        "rationales": [
          {"option_id": "A", "truth": "incorrect", "derivation": "Deduplicating the two Literature entries leaves five subjects, but does not remove a numbered position.", "misconception": "Count distinct subjects rather than the six positions."},
          {"option_id": "B", "truth": "incorrect", "derivation": "The period labels differ, but values at periods 3 and 4 are both Literature.", "misconception": "Transfer the distinctness of indices to the associated function values."},
          {"option_id": "C", "truth": "correct", "derivation": "There are six period columns and equal Literature values at positions 3 and 4.", "misconception": null},
          {"option_id": "D", "truth": "incorrect", "derivation": "The table has seven columns including the heading column; only the six numbered columns are terms.", "misconception": "Count the Subject heading as an additional sequence value."}
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "q190-schedules",
      "source_numbers": ["190"],
      "view": {
        "mode": "multiple",
        "stem": "三年级一天有四节课，课表必须包含体育、英语、数学、自然四门课。下面哪些课表方案符合要求？每个方案按第 1 至第 4 节排列。",
        "figure_ids": [],
        "options": [
          {"id": "A", "text": "体育，英语，数学，自然", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "B", "text": "英语，体育，自然，数学", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "C", "text": "体育，英语，数学，数学", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "D", "text": "数学，自然，英语，体育", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "E", "text": "体育，英语，自然", "figure_ids": []}
        ]
      },
      "intent": {
        "task": "Recognize several ordered four-subject schedules containing every required subject.",
        "source_solution": "Valid schedules are permutations of the four subjects: each must occur exactly once in four slots. A,B,D are three independently valid examples; there are 24 possibilities, not all requested.",
        "unit_reason": "Each option is an entire schedule, and native multiple selection retains the request for several plans rather than choosing a combination code.",
        "concept_blocks": [5,7],
        "limitations": ["The written task requires inventing several schedules; selection only demonstrates recognizing offered permutations.", "Ability to generate other valid orders is not measured; enumeration of all 24 was never required."],
        "figure_observations": []
      },
      "key": {
        "correct": ["A","B","D"],
        "rationales": [
          {"option_id": "A", "truth": "correct", "derivation": "Four positions contain the four required subjects exactly once.", "misconception": null},
          {"option_id": "B", "truth": "correct", "derivation": "Changing order does not remove a subject; the four required subjects each occur once.", "misconception": null},
          {"option_id": "C", "truth": "incorrect", "derivation": "Copying Mathematics into the fourth slot duplicates it and omits Nature.", "misconception": "Check only the number of slots and permit a repeated course to replace a required course."},
          {"option_id": "D", "truth": "correct", "derivation": "This is another permutation of the same four subjects, with all four present.", "misconception": null},
          {"option_id": "E", "truth": "incorrect", "derivation": "Dropping Mathematics yields only three positions and lacks a required subject.", "misconception": "Stop after listing three allowed subjects without checking length and full inclusion."}
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "q191-odd-map",
      "source_numbers": ["191"],
      "view": {
        "mode": "single",
        "stem": "有限数列 $1,3,5,7,9$ 是定义域为 $X$、值域为 $Y$ 的函数。哪份完整表示正确？其中数对 $(i,v)$ 表示箭头 $i\\mapsto v$。",
        "figure_ids": [],
        "options": [
          {"id": "A", "text": "$X=\\{1,3,5,7,9\\},\\ Y=\\{1,2,3,4,5\\}$；数对为 $\\{(1,1),(3,2),(5,3),(7,4),(9,5)\\}$。", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "B", "text": "$X=\\{1,2,3,4,5\\},\\ Y=\\{1,3,5,7,9\\}$；数对为 $\\{(1,1),(2,3),(3,5),(4,7),(5,9)\\}$。", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "C", "text": "$X=\\{0,1,2,3,4\\},\\ Y=\\{1,3,5,7,9\\}$；数对为 $\\{(0,1),(1,3),(2,5),(3,7),(4,9)\\}$。", "figure_ids": []}
        ]
      },
      "intent": {
        "task": "Determine the domain, range and every directed index-to-term association of the odd-valued finite function.",
        "source_solution": "X={1,2,3,4,5}; Y={1,3,5,7,9}; pairs (1,1),(2,3),(3,5),(4,7),(5,9), equivalently arrows 1->1,2->3,3->5,4->7,5->9.",
        "unit_reason": "A whole function representation tests direction, order and domain together. The three source functions have genuinely different value patterns, so each gets its own complete representation, not per-cell questions.",
        "concept_blocks": [5,7,8,9],
        "limitations": ["Writing the sets and pairs independently is replaced by recognition.", "Every arrow's endpoints and direction are retained via ordered-pair equivalence; spatial arrow-diagram construction and separately writing all arrows are not tested."],
        "figure_observations": []
      },
      "key": {
        "correct": ["B"],
        "rationales": [
          {"option_id": "A", "truth": "incorrect", "derivation": "Swapping each pair's components gives the inverse relation and interchanges X and Y.", "misconception": "Map term values to positions instead of positions to term values."},
          {"option_id": "B", "truth": "correct", "derivation": "The five first positive positions map in order to 1,3,5,7,9; their images form Y.", "misconception": null},
          {"option_id": "C", "truth": "incorrect", "derivation": "Subtracting 1 from every position places the first term at position 0.", "misconception": "Use zero-based array indices instead of the seeded first-term convention."}
        ]
      }
    },
    {
