    {
      "id": "q199-round-seven",
      "source_numbers": ["199"],
      "view": {
        "mode": "single",
        "stem": "把 $\\frac7{12}$ 写成无穷小数，并依次四舍五入到十分位、百分位、千分位等，得到数列 $(x_n)$，第 $n$ 项保留 $n$ 位小数。哪份完整分析正确？",
        "figure_ids": [],
        "options": [
          {"id": "A", "text": "$\\frac7{12}=0.58\\overline3$；$x_1=0.5,x_2=0.58,x_3=0.583,x_{10}=0.5833333333$；没有相同项；是增数列。", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "B", "text": "$\\frac7{12}=0.58\\overline3$；$x_1=0.6,x_2=0.58,x_3=0.583,x_{10}=0.5833333333$；没有相同项；既非增数列也非减数列。", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "C", "text": "$\\frac7{12}=0.58\\overline3$；$x_1=0.6,x_2=0.59,x_3=0.584,x_{10}=0.5833333334$；没有相同项；是减数列。", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "D", "text": "$\\frac7{12}=0.58\\overline3$；$x_1=0.6,x_2=0.58,x_3=0.583,x_{10}=0.5833333333$；没有相同项；是减数列。", "figure_ids": []}
        ]
      },
      "intent": {
        "task": "Convert the fraction, round at four requested precisions, assess repeated values and classify the complete sequence.",
        "source_solution": "7/12=0.583333...; x1=.6,x2=.58,x3=.583,x10=.5833333333. For n>=2 the following digit 3 gives truncation and each added 3 strictly increases the term. x2<x1 but x3>x2; no repeats, neither monotone category.",
        "unit_reason": "A whole rounding-process analysis joins the numerical values to the global trend; it is not four disconnected rounding answers.",
        "concept_blocks": [7,8,12,15,16,18],
        "limitations": ["Independent long division, rounding calculations and written trend proof are replaced by recognizing a complete analysis.", "The neither category is retained despite the source's increase-or-decrease wording; no false binary classification is imposed."],
        "figure_observations": []
      },
      "key": {
        "correct": ["B"],
        "rationales": [
          {"option_id": "A", "truth": "incorrect", "derivation": "Truncate at every precision instead of rounding: .5,.58,.583,... then strictly increase. The first result must round up because its next digit is 8.", "misconception": "Replace round-to-nearest by truncation, changing both x1 and the global trend."},
          {"option_id": "B", "truth": "correct", "derivation": "Division yields .58 followed by repeating 3. Next digit 8 rounds the first term to .6; all later next digits 3 preserve truncations. Later terms are distinct and increasing below .6, so the initial fall precludes increase and later rises preclude decrease.", "misconception": null},
          {"option_id": "C", "truth": "incorrect", "derivation": "Always increase the last retained digit whenever discarded digits are nonzero: ceiling gives .6,.59,.584,..., a decreasing sequence, but is not four舍五入.", "misconception": "Use directed upward rounding instead of checking whether the next digit is at least 5."},
          {"option_id": "D", "truth": "incorrect", "derivation": "The displayed values are correct, but x3=.583>.58=x2 contradicts decreasing.", "misconception": "Classify the entire sequence from only the first decrease x1 to x2."}
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "q199-round-twentythree",
      "source_numbers": ["199"],
      "view": {
        "mode": "single",
        "stem": "把 $\\frac{23}{45}$ 写成无穷小数，依次四舍五入到十分位、百分位、千分位等得到 $(y_n)$。哪项同时给出无穷小数、等于 $0.5111111111$ 的项和整个数列的增减性质？",
        "figure_ids": [],
        "options": [
          {"id": "A", "text": "$\\frac{23}{45}=0.5\\overline1$；$y_{11}=0.5111111111$；$(y_n)$ 是增数列。", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "B", "text": "$\\frac{23}{45}=0.5\\overline1$；$y_{10}=0.5111111111$；$(y_n)$ 是减数列。", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "C", "text": "$\\frac{23}{45}=0.5\\overline1$；$y_{10}=0.5111111111$；$(y_n)$ 是增数列。", "figure_ids": []}
        ]
      },
      "intent": {
        "task": "Convert the second fraction, infer the requested term's index from precision and judge the infinite rounding sequence.",
        "source_solution": "23/45=.511111... . All next discarded digits are 1, so y_n retains n decimal digits without upward rounding. .5111111111 has ten fractional digits and is y10. Each next term adds 10^(-(n+1)) for n>=1 and strictly increases.",
        "unit_reason": "This fraction has a different rounding pattern from 7/12; one complete decimal/index/trend assertion retains its own full task.",
        "concept_blocks": [7,8,12,15,16,18],
        "limitations": ["Division, digit counting and the adjacent-difference proof are recognized rather than independently written."],
        "figure_observations": []
      },
      "key": {
        "correct": ["C"],
        "rationales": [
          {"option_id": "A", "truth": "incorrect", "derivation": "Count the leading integer 0 along with the ten fractional digits to get eleven, but indices count retained decimal places only.", "misconception": "Include the integer digit in the rounding-precision count."},
          {"option_id": "B", "truth": "incorrect", "derivation": "The first two terms .5 and .51 already satisfy .51>.5; every later appended 1 also increases the value.", "misconception": "Assume additional decimal places make the number smaller without comparing values."},
          {"option_id": "C", "truth": "correct", "derivation": "45*.5=22.5, leaving .5/45=.011111...; ten fractional digits yield y10 and each additional 1 creates a positive increment.", "misconception": null}
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "q200-descending-graph",
      "source_numbers": ["200"],
      "view": {
